# v301 — SHARED BROWSER TRANSPORT
# Test infrastructure only: one PostgreSQL transport helper, consumed by the
# seven browser suites that need a database. No SQL object, no migration.
#
# It still carries a manifest, for the reason v296 states: a release that ships
# no SQL is still a release, and the chain must not break at it. Its prerequisite
# is the whole chain beneath it — and in this release's case that is more than a
# formality, because the suites it repairs are the ones that PROVE the chain.
release          v301
migration
migration_source none
min_release      v300
